Nexos wrote:
>
> I play an Orcist barbarian and wonder which dragon scale mail to wear.

Gray gives magic resistance and thus frees up your [oMR allowing
you to replace it with a robe or protection or other cloak.  It is
arguably the best piece of armor available for that reason.

Silver gives reflection and thus frees up either "oR or [oR allowing
you to wear lifesaving or go shieldless.  It ranks second in
popularity for the best piece of armor available.

If you get a wish, one of those two is the thing to wish for most
of the time.

> I just got to Fort Ludios, killed some dragons and red, blue and white
> dragon scales are lying on the ground.
>
> I've also two pets polymorphed into silver and black dragon
> respectively.

Red, blue, white and black all confer resistances that you get from
eating that color dragon corpse so in reality all they do is give
excellent AC for little weight.  Pick you favorite color.  You could
try killing your silver dragon for the scales but there's a low chance
of any one dragon giving scales and revived dragons apparently
have even lower chances.  I've burned through a couple of wands
of undead turning without getting a scale.  Arguably your dragon
pets are worth more alive than dead.  Your black one is almost
certainly worth more alive than dead since you already have
disintegration resistance:

> I've got all resistances (including disintegration) and currently wear
> a fireproof cloak of magic resistance above my elven-mithril coat.
>
> I've also an amulet of reflection (Sokoban)
>
> Should I wear any of the scales on the ground, or kill one of my pets
> to get its "skin" (so I can put off my amulet and put one of life
> saving) ?

Style issues - Red is the traditional Norse/Germanic color.  It's
why Santa Claus wears red.  Thus red mail is for Valks.  Black is
for the goth set, and that works okay as a barbarian.  Green
is the traditional Druidic color and your don't have green but
blue.  Maybe you have green/blue color blindness.  White seems
more civilized.  It isn't quite worth killing a pet for just a chance
of the scale, so go for red or blue.  And keep watching for either
gray or silver dragons or for a wish.



